The native binaries of jazzclub embed libjsound, the native part of Java Sound,
taken unmodified from the OpenJDK build of GraalVM Community Edition. It is
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 with the Classpath
Exception; source code is available from https://github.com/openjdk/jdk and
https://github.com/graalvm/graalvm-ce-builds.

jazzclub's built-in audio decoder uses parts of LavaPlayer 2.2.7
(https://github.com/lavalink-devs/lavaplayer), Copyright its contributors,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (licenses/lavaplayer.txt). Its Java MP4
parser and AAC decoder binding are compiled into jazzclub.

The decoder's native library, libconnector, is LavaPlayer's prebuilt
lavaplayer-natives 2.2.7, shipped unmodified as a separate shared library
(/usr/lib/jazzclub/ on Linux, libexec/jazzclub/ on macOS; the native binary
also embeds a copy). Besides LavaPlayer's own JNI code it contains, statically
linked:

  - Fraunhofer FDK AAC Codec Library 2.0.0
    (https://github.com/mstorsjo/fdk-aac), under the Software License for The
    Fraunhofer FDK AAC Codec Library for Android (licenses/fdk-aac.txt).
    This licence permits redistribution but is not considered free software
    by Debian or Fedora. Patent licences for AAC are not granted by it.
  - mpg123 1.25.10 (https://www.mpg123.de), Copyright (c) 1995-2013 by
    Michael Hipp and others, under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1
    (licenses/mpg123.txt). Its source is available from
    https://www.mpg123.de/download/mpg123-1.25.10.tar.bz2. LavaPlayer's source
    and build scripts for libconnector are at
    https://github.com/lavalink-devs/lavaplayer/tree/2.2.7/natives, so the
    library can be rebuilt with a modified mpg123 and dropped in place of the
    installed file.
  - Opus 1.3 (https://opus-codec.org), BSD licence (licenses/opus.txt).
  - libogg 1.3.3 and libvorbis 1.3.6 (https://xiph.org), BSD licence
    (licenses/libogg.txt, licenses/libvorbis.txt).
  - libsamplerate 0.1.9 (https://github.com/libsndfile/libsamplerate),
    BSD licence (licenses/libsamplerate.txt).

jazzclub uses only the AAC decoder; the other codecs come with the library.

